{
  "name": "Dealing with Loose Kitchen Tiles and Mats",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Loose kitchen tiles and curled-up mats? Those are classic trip hazards just waiting to happen. You know, you're walking along, not really paying attention, and *bam*! You've got a problem. Let's break down how to tackle these. First off, get those loose or sliding mats out of the way. If you really need mats, invest in ones with secure, slip-resistant backing. You want them to stay put, not slide around like a hockey puck. For damaged or raised tiles, that's a fix you shouldn't put off. Ignoring them is a big mistake. If it’s just one or two, you might try a DIY repair, but if you have a lot of uneven flooring or bigger sections of broken tiles, that's when a professional like HH Remodeling LLC comes in handy. We can assess the situation and ensure the repair is done right, preventing future trips and falls. Don't let your kitchen be a hazard zone; it’s too important a space. Reach out to us at 303-505-0866 for help.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
